SELAHCUE DEVELOPMENT ENTITLEMENT SIGNING SEED — DELIBERATELY PUBLIC, NEVER PRODUCTION
=====================================================================================

Ed25519 seed (32 bytes, ASCII):  SELAHCUE-DEV-ONLY-NOT-A-SECRET!!
Public key  (32 bytes, decimal): 122,63,108,222,26,234,144,88,16,53,82,180,127,244,213,16,
                                 86,6,76,132,249,209,18,122,21,96,175,100,231,174,33,129
key_id (SHA-256 of the public key, first 8 hex): f5194d13

WHAT THIS IS FOR
`make launch` / `make output` / `make operator` must not demand activation or an account:
development cannot be gated on the licensing stack, and the owner will opt into QAing
enforcement deliberately. The chosen mechanism is to MINT, not to bypass.

WHY MINT RATHER THAN BYPASS
A bypass is a branch in the enforcement path that skips verification, and that branch is the
highest-value target in the product: anything that flips it — an env var, a config file, a
flag found in `strings` — hands out unlimited entitlement. It also means the path we ship is
not the path anyone develops against, so the first real QA is the first time the code has
ever run.

DEC-011 already supplies the clean answer: the client trusts a SET of public keys and the
manifest names one by `key_id`. So a debug build additionally trusts the key above, `make`
mints a dev-signed manifest carrying `key_id = f5194d13`, and real verification runs — real
signature checking, real expiry, real cache behaviour. There is no bypass branch to find.

WHY THIS SEED IS COMMITTED
Because it must be impossible to mistake for a production secret. A secret that is
deliberately public cannot be confused with one that leaked, and the seed is readable ASCII
that says so. Release builds do NOT trust the corresponding public key — see
`TrustedKeys::bundled` and `the_development_key_is_gated_on_debug_assertions` in
`tests/test_trust.rs`, which fails if that gate is removed.

The production signing key is an env-var seed on the server
(`SELAHCUE_ENTITLEMENT_SIGNING_KEY`, DEC-011 pt 1) and has no relationship to this file.
